@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam noteFontSize 12
skinparam participantPadding 30

title LLM APIs Are Stateless — Every Call Resends Everything

participant "Your Code\n(chatlas)" as Client
participant "LLM API\n(GitHub Models)" as API
database "chat object\n(local memory)" as Memory

== Turn 1 ==

Client -> Memory : store user message
Client -> API : **Request 1**\n[system] You are a terse assistant.\n[user] What is the capital of the moon?
note right of API : 25 tokens sent
API --> Client : [assistant] The moon has no capital.
Client -> Memory : store assistant reply

== Turn 2 ==

Client -> Memory : store user message
Client -> API : **Request 2**\n[system] You are a terse assistant.\n[user] What is the capital of the moon?\n[assistant] The moon has no capital.\n[user] **Are you sure?**
note right of API : 52 tokens sent\n(11 new + 41 repeated)
API --> Client : [assistant] Yes, I am sure.
Client -> Memory : store assistant reply

== Turn 3 ==

Client -> Memory : store user message
Client -> API : **Request 3**\n[system] You are a terse assistant.\n[user] What is the capital of the moon?\n[assistant] The moon has no capital.\n[user] Are you sure?\n[assistant] Yes, I am sure.\n[user] **Tell me a fun moon fact.**
note right of API : 104 tokens sent\n(31 new + 73 repeated)
API --> Client : [assistant] The moon has moonquakes...
Client -> Memory : store assistant reply

note over Client, API
  The API has **no memory** between calls.
  The chat object rebuilds the full context every time.
  Cost grows with conversation length!
end note

@enduml
